# The app icon picked in Settings never goes on Cra.app itself (GitHub #724). 0.1.54 and 0.1.55 put it there as
# Finder's custom icon (an Icon\r file and a com.apple.FinderInfo flag), as Arc does, so Finder showed it. That
# attribute on the bundle breaks the app's signature: `codesign --strict` refuses it, and lsd kept registering the
# app launch-disabled. The Dock tile shows the pick (app-icon-segments-dock); the bundle stays as it was signed.
# Midnight comes in through the argument domain and appIcon= picks without remembering, so the run never writes the
# defaults the installed Cra reads. strict= is what `codesign --verify --strict` says of the app.
# promise: #724
home
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true}
arg -appIcon
arg midnight
cra://debug?bundleIcon=launch
expect-log bundle icon launch: custom=0 file=0 strict=valid$
cra://debug?appIcon=mono
cra://debug?bundleIcon=mono
expect-log bundle icon mono: custom=0 file=0 strict=valid$
reject-log put on the app$

# A Finder icon 0.1.54 or 0.1.55 left on the app comes off at the next launch, and the signature holds again.
cra://debug?bundleIconPut=midnight
expect-log app icon: midnight put on the app for a test
cra://debug?bundleIcon=leftover
expect-log bundle icon leftover: custom=1 file=1 strict=-66999$
relaunch
expect-log app icon: \S+ taken off the app
cra://debug?bundleIcon=relaunched
expect-log bundle icon relaunched: custom=0 file=0 strict=valid$
